{"name":"Threaded Loom","hex":"#cec2aa","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"threaded","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having threads.","Of messages: arranged in a thread or threads."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of thread"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/threaded"},{"term":"loom","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A utensil; tool; a weapon;  an article in general.","A frame or machine of wood or other material, in which a weaver forms cloth out of thread; a machine for interweaving yarn or threads into a fabric, as in knitting or lace making."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["loon (bird of order Gaviiformes)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loom"}],"entries":[{"title":"Loom","blocks":[{"text":"A loom is a device used to weave cloth and tapestry. The basic purpose of any loom is to hold the warp threads under tension to facilitate the interweaving of the weft threads. The precise shape of the loom and its mechanics may vary, but the basic function is the same."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Loom_2%2C_Lesbos_%28Skala_Sykamias%29.jpg/330px-Loom_2%2C_Lesbos_%28Skala_Sykamias%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loom","wikidata":"Q173056"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Pedal-driven-weaving-machine.jpg/500px-Pedal-driven-weaving-machine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Pedal-driven-weaving-machine.jpg/1280px-Pedal-driven-weaving-machine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Pedal-driven-weaving-machine.jpg/500px-Pedal-driven-weaving-machine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A treadle-driven Hattersley & Sons Domestic \nLoom, built under licence in 1893, in Keighley, Yorkshire. This loom has a flying shuttle and automatically rolls up the woven cloth; it is not just controlled but powered by the pedals.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APedal-driven-weaving-machine.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Simple_treadle_floorloom%2C_line_drawing.png/500px-Simple_treadle_floorloom%2C_line_drawing.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Simple_treadle_floorloom%2C_line_drawing.png/1280px-Simple_treadle_floorloom%2C_line_drawing.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Simple_treadle_floorloom%2C_line_drawing.png/500px-Simple_treadle_floorloom%2C_line_drawing.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A simple treadle floor loom. Mouse over components for pop-up links. The warp runs horizontally. On the left the warp beam, held from turning by with a weighted trough to keep the warp taut; on the right, the cloth beam (also called a breast beam on this type of loom), with a pawl and ratchet to allow the weaver to roll up the fell. In the center, devices for performing the motions of weaving.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASimple_treadle_floorloom%2C_line_drawing.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Tropenmuseum_Royal_Tropical_Institute_Objectnumber_403-150_Toestel_voor_het_vervaardigen_van_kral.jpg/500px-Tropenmuseum_Royal_Tropical_Institute_Objectnumber_403-150_Toestel_voor_het_vervaardigen_van_kral.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Tropenmuseum_Royal_Tropical_Institute_Objectnumber_403-150_Toestel_voor_het_vervaardigen_van_kral.jpg/500px-Tropenmuseum_Royal_Tropical_Institute_Objectnumber_403-150_Toestel_voor_het_vervaardigen_van_kral.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A simple handheld frame loom","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATropenmuseum_Royal_Tropical_Institute_Objectnumber_403-150_Toestel_voor_het_vervaardigen_van_kral.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Belarus_weaving.jpg/500px-Belarus_weaving.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Belarus_weaving.jpg/1280px-Belarus_weaving.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Belarus_weaving.jpg/500px-Belarus_weaving.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Passing the shuttle through the shed","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABelarus_weaving.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/WEAVING_WITH_A_PIN_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-WEAVING_WITH_A_PIN_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/WEAVING_WITH_A_PIN_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-WEAVING_WITH_A_PIN_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/WEAVING_WITH_A_PIN_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-WEAVING_WITH_A_PIN_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pin weaving, not using any shedding devices. Note ordinary white plastic hair comb (beneath a red yarn, behind the box), presumably used to beat the warp against the fell.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWEAVING_WITH_A_PIN_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Lisses_du_m%C3%A9tier_%C3%A0_tisser.jpg/500px-Lisses_du_m%C3%A9tier_%C3%A0_tisser.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Lisses_du_m%C3%A9tier_%C3%A0_tisser.jpg/1280px-Lisses_du_m%C3%A9tier_%C3%A0_tisser.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Lisses_du_m%C3%A9tier_%C3%A0_tisser.jpg/500px-Lisses_du_m%C3%A9tier_%C3%A0_tisser.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Heddle-rod, laid across the warp threads, and tied to every other thread with short lengths of string. Tapestry loom, France, 2018","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALisses_du_m%C3%A9tier_%C3%A0_tisser.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/M%C3%A9tier_vertical_%C3%A0_pesons_2.jpg/500px-M%C3%A9tier_vertical_%C3%A0_pesons_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/M%C3%A9tier_vertical_%C3%A0_pesons_2.jpg/1280px-M%C3%A9tier_vertical_%C3%A0_pesons_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/M%C3%A9tier_vertical_%C3%A0_pesons_2.jpg/500px-M%C3%A9tier_vertical_%C3%A0_pesons_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AM%C3%A9tier_vertical_%C3%A0_pesons_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/22/Spede%2BWeve%2BMiniature%2BLoom%2BModel%2B1%2BInstructions_%28cropped_to_illustration%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/22/Spede%2BWeve%2BMiniature%2BLoom%2BModel%2B1%2BI